  "_meta": {
    "version": "starter",
    "last_updated": "2026-04-21",
    "purpose": "Vendor-to-category map used by v2's category-aware fallback. When a user pitches a vendor at an agency and the direct pull returns zero rows, this file tells the fallback WHICH category keywords to search for at that agency. Without it, the fallback would drop to agency-wide data (e.g., border-wall construction for a SentinelOne query at DHS) — which is wrong. Keys are lowercased vendor names. Values carry category (for display), keywords (what to search USASpending for), and competitors (for future competitor-chip generation). Keywords should match USASpending's actual description vocabulary — what contracts ACTUALLY say, not marketing terms. For example: USASpending descriptions use 'ENDPOINT DETECTION' and 'EDR', not 'endpoint security'."
  },
